# [FABLE-5] sq-hmd7l.29 — Geographica real-world micro NON-TOPOLOGICAL query
# "QUERY 4 - Buffer_GeoNames" (micro_nontopological.lst, geographica2.di.uoa.gr), pinned for
# scripts/bench/geo-same-box.sh (the GEO_GEOGRAPHICA=1 family; corpus recipe
# bench/geo/geographica.sh). TRANSLATIONS vs upstream (see bench/geo/README.md):
#   * GRAPH <http://geographica.di.uoa.gr/dataset/...> wrapper dropped — both
#     engines load the merged slice into the default graph; the per-dataset
#     predicate IRIs keep LGD/GeoNames distinguishable.
#   * COUNT-wrapped (counts-not-coordinates): only the result-set SIZE is
#     cross-checked between engines before any timing is trusted.
#   * upstream 2-arg Strabon-dialect buffer(?o1, r) -> the standard 3-arg
#     geof:buffer(?o1, r, uom:degree): the same planar degree-space semantic,
#     executable identically on both engines (no degree->metre conversion).
#   * COUNT(?ret) counts only rows where the function EVALUATED (an error
#     leaves ?ret unbound), so the count is a per-engine function-evaluation
#     oracle and the HTTP response stays tiny (no giant WKT serialisation
#     across the recorded in-process-vs-HTTP mode asymmetry).
# Oracle: COUNT must equal expected-geographica.tsv before timing is trusted.
PREFIX geof: <http://www.opengis.net/def/function/geosparql/>
PREFIX uom:  <http://www.opengis.net/def/uom/OGC/1.0/>
SELECT (COUNT(?ret) AS ?n) WHERE {
  ?s1 <http://www.geonames.org/ontology#asWKT> ?o1 .
  BIND(geof:buffer(?o1, 0.04, uom:degree) AS ?ret)
}
